<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ballal Sena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1179</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ballalasena, Ballala Sena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ballal Sena was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-dynasty">Sena dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> who ruled in the 12th century, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayasena">Vijayasena</a>. Tradition credits him with organising the ranking of Bengali <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">castes</a> known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulinism">Kulinism</a>. He wrote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> works on ritual and omens, including the Danasagara, while the Adbhutasagara he began was completed by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshman-sena">Lakshman Sena</a>.</p></div>
